        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare visceral arteriovenous malformation characterized by direct arterial-to-venous connections within the liver. Patients may be asymptomatic or present with symptoms such as anemia consumptive coagulopathy portal hypertension hepatomegaly and may develop complications including congestive heart failure necrosis of the liver or hydrops fetalis."
        },
